The attached image displays the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles, which are dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucans. The left panel shows a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image, indicating the nanoparticles are spherical with an irregular, "cauliflower-like" appearance, mostly individual or in small aggregates, with a scale bar of 50 nm. The right panel is a dynamic light scattering histogram, demonstrating a narrow size distribution with a peak between 70-80 nm, consistent with the Z-average hydrodynamic diameter ranging from 75 to 80 nm as discussed in the PDF, affirming their uniform size for efficient cellular uptake.